ump-typed-clang-ast\n            Prints out the parsed typed Clang AST\n\n        --dump-untyped-clang-ast\n            Prints out CBOR based Clang AST\n\n    -e, --emit-build-files\n            Emit Rust build files, i.e., Cargo.toml for a library (and one or more binaries if\n            -b/--binary is given). Implies --emit-modules\n\n        --emit-c-decl-map\n            Write map of C decls corresponding to each translated Rust item alongside the transpiled\n            output with the extension `.c_decls.json`\n\n        --emit-modules\n            Emit .rs files as modules instead of crates, excluding the crate preambles\n\n        --emit-no-std\n            Emit code using core rather than std\n\n    -f, --filter <FILTER>\n            Only transpile files matching filter\n\n        --fail-on-error\n            Fail to translate a module when a portion is not able to be translated\n\n        --fail-on-multiple\n            Fail when the control-flow graph generates branching constructs\n\n    -h, --help\n            Print help information\n\n        --ignore-c-loop-info\n            Don't keep/use information about C loops\n\n        --ignore-c-multiple-info\n            Don't keep/use information about C branches\n\n        --invalid-code <INVALID_CODE>\n            How to handle violated invariants or invalid code [default: compile_error] [possible\n            values: panic, compile_error]\n\n        --json-function-cfgs\n            Dumps into files JSON visualizations of the CFGs of every function\n\n        --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>\n            Logging level [default: WARN]\n\n        --no-incremental-relooper\n            Disable relooping function bodies incrementally\n\n        --no-simplify-structures\n            Do not run a pass to simplify structures\n\n    -o, --output-dir <DIR>\n            Path to output directory. Rust sources will be emitted in DIR/src/ and build files will\n            be emitted in DIR/\n\n        --overwrite-existing\n  